=== Decode each to SG Case-II (p,q) and apply face/Pi test ===
p = Y,  q = (Y^2 + 2Y - 1)/2;  Case-B legs:
  a = 4 p q,   b = q^2 - 4 p^2,   c = 2(q^2 - p^2)
Face/Pi value (third-face squareness) = 5 q^4 - 16 p^2 q^2 + 20 p^4

  Y=-1 -> (p,q)=(-1,-1)  legs (a,b,c)=(4,-3,0)
       Face/Pi = 9   square? 1   degenerate? 1
  Y=1 -> (p,q)=(1,1)  legs (a,b,c)=(4,-3,0)
       Face/Pi = 9   square? 1   degenerate? 1
  Y=11 -> (p,q)=(11,71)  legs (a,b,c)=(3124,4557,9840)
       Face/Pi = 117591849   square? 0   degenerate? 0

=== The single non-degenerate candidate (p,q)=(11,71) ===
Face/Pi = 117591849
sqrtint(Face/Pi) = 10843,  sqrtint^2 = 117570649
issquare? 0   (must be 0 = NOT a square)
So no perfect cuboid arises from (11,71): the third face fails squareness.

